"short","prompt":"Your friend writes “I bringed my lunch.” Explain the mistake and how to fix it.","rubric":["Says “bring” is irregular and doesn’t take -ed","Gives the correct form: “I brought my lunch.”"],"model":"“Bring” is an irregular verb, so its past tense isn’t made with -ed. The sentence should be “I brought my lunch.”","text":"bring is irregular so you dont add ed. it should be I brought my lunch.","at":"@T4@10:22:00","where":"practice"},{"id":"wdemo3","qid":"verbs:perfectAspect:short","courseId":"verbs","skillId":"perfectAspect","type":"short","prompt":"Explain the difference between “I ate lunch” and “I have eaten lunch.”","rubric":["Says “I ate lunch” tells about a finished time in the past","Says “I have eaten lunch” connects the past action to now (it’s done as of now)"],"model":"“I ate lunch” tells what happened at a finished time in the past. “I have eaten lunch” connects that action to now: right now, I am not hungry because lunch is done.","text":"I ate lunch is just in the past. I have eaten lunch means I ate it and it still matters now, like I am not hungry.","at":"@M77","where":"practice"}],"readingBooks":[{"id":"book-1","title":"The Wild Robot","author":"Peter Brown","chapters":[{"id":"ch1","label":"Chapters 1–5","characters":"Roz, the otters","notableAction":"Roz turns on for the first time on the island after the storm.","interaction":"","conflict":"Roz doesn't know where she is or what she is for.","joy":"I liked how it started right away with something big happening.","setting":"","themes":"Being brave when you are scared.","detail":"","vocabulary":"","submittedAt":"@T20@14:00:00","localReview":"verified","updatedAt":"@T20@14:00:00"},{"id":"ch2","label":"Chapters 6–10","characters":"Roz, the bear","notableAction":"Roz watches the animals to learn how they survive.","interaction":"","conflict":"The animals think she is a monster.","joy":"","setting":"","themes":"","detail":"","vocabulary":"","submittedAt":"@T14@14:01:00","localReview":"","u